# Changing this file on a push runs the Records workflow: other sources' records about the place.
# With AREA, the box round that area's wards (data/areas.json), keeping only the records inside them,
# from the newest SNAPSHOT_NAME snapshot. The file is read as shell: quote a name with a space (AREA="South Norwood").
# RECORDS_OUT puts a place's records in its own folder, which Croydon's build never reads.
# Kenilworth, Warwickshire: every source that covers England (not London's planning or trees).
# Asked again for the three whose services failed last time (listed buildings 503, Land Registry 403,
# flood zones timed out); the rest are in.
# (Croydon's last: SNAPSHOT_NAME=croydon AREA="South Norwood".)
SNAPSHOT_NAME=kenilworth
RECORDS_OUT=data/records/kenilworth
SOURCES=protected,prices,floodzones
